    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the negative integers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the negative integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}^{+}$ contains the positive rational numbers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Q}^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}^{+}$ contains the positive real numbers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}_0$ contains the nonnegative integers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{N}_0$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative integers.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ only.",
